SUMMARY:NEW EVENT - 👻🌙 The Ghosts of Cabbagetown
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 👻
 🌙 The Ghosts of Cabbagetown\n\n### A 90-Minute Evening Ghost Walk Throu
 gh One of Toronto’s Most Historic Neighbourhoods\n\nCabbagetown has beau
 tiful Victorian houses\, quiet streets\, old cemeteries\, and a history th
 at goes back generations.\nIt also has ghosts.\n\nJoin me for a **90-minut
 e evening walking tour through Cabbagetown**\, where we'll explore some of
  the neighbourhood's strangest stories\, unsettling legends\, and darker p
 ieces of Toronto's past.\n\nWe'll begin beneath the glass of **Allan Garde
 ns**\, then make our way through the streets of Cabbagetown\, stopping alo
 ng the way for stories of mysterious creatures\, haunted buildings\, old p
 risons\, cemeteries\, restless spirits\, and the people who may never have
  quite left.\nThis isn't a traditional history walk.\n\nIt's a **ghost tou
 r** — so expect some history\, some local legends\, a little mystery\, a
 nd a few stories that are difficult to explain.\nAnd\, of course\, we'll h
 ave a few laughs along the way.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsAp
 p Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)
 **\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Explore\n\nOur route will take us through 
 some of Cabbagetown's most atmospheric locations\, including:\n🌿 **Alla
 n Gardens** — ghosts beneath the glass\n🐾 **Winchester Square Park** 
 — the strange story of Cabbagetown's Tunnel Monster\n🍸 **The Winchest
 er Hotel** — spirits that may have never checked out\n🏚️ **Winchest
 er Street** — haunted houses and Victorian secrets\n⛓️ **The Don Jai
 l & Bridgepoint** — where the walls remember everything\n🐄 **Riverdal
 e Farm** — and its strange connection to the old Don Jail\n⚰️ **The 
 Toronto Necropolis** — a city of the dead beneath a city of the living\n
 🕯️ **St. James Town & St. James' Cemetery** — where the living and 
 the dead share the same neighbourhood\nAnd much\, much more...\n\n***\n\n#
 # 🌙 What Makes This Tour Different?\n\nThis is a **new ghost walk for t
 he group**\, created specifically around Cabbagetown.\nRather than simply 
 walking from one location to another\, the route has been **curated around
  the stories** so that each stop connects to the next.\n\nWe'll move throu
 gh the neighbourhood at a comfortable pace\, stopping along the way while 
 I share the stories behind the places we're visiting.\nSome stories are hi
 storical.\nSome are local legends.\nSome are downright strange.\nYou'll ha
 ve to decide for yourself which ones you believe. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🕯
 ️ A Little About the Tour\n\nThis is a **90-minute evening walk**.\nWe w
 ill be walking outdoors throughout the tour and will **not be entering bui
 ldings**.\nSome locations may be viewed from outside or from nearby public
  spaces.\nPlease be respectful of residents\, private property\, and cemet
 ery grounds as we make our way through the neighbourhood.\n\n***\n\n## 
 📍 Meetup Details\n\n🕚 **Meeting Time:** 6:30 PM\nI will only wait **
 5 minutes** before we begin.\n🫎 **Meeting Location:** Outside the **Pal
 m House at Allan Gardens (this BIG WHITE building)**\nLook for me in my **
 Moose Hat!**\n🏁 **End Point:** Parliament Street & Wellesley Street Eas
 t\n🚶 **Walking Time:** Approximately 90 minutes\n👻 **Pace:** Comfort
 able\, steady walking pace\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash o
 r e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@ho
 tmail.com)**\nThe $10 fee helps support the group and covers the **extra r
 esearch\, preparation\, and curation that goes into creating these ghost w
 alks**.\nThese aren't simply walks where we meet up and wander around.\nI'
 ve put together a specific route\, researched the stories\, and created a 
 series of stops designed to turn the walk into an actual **storytelling ex
 perience**.\nYou're paying for the experience — not just the walking.\n\
 n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weat
 her-appropriate clothing\n💧 Water\n🔦 A little extra light if you hav
 e it\n👻 An open mind\nAnd maybe don't wander off by yourself.\nYou neve
 r know who's walking behind you.\n\n***\n\n## ⚠️ A Quick Note\n\nSomet
 imes things happen and I may need to cancel or change an event.\nPlease ke
 ep an eye on the event page for updates.\nYou can RSVP ahead of time — o
 r **just show up on the day if you're not sure about your schedule.**\n\n*
 **\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is for anyone who enjoys:\n
 👻 Ghost stories and local legends\n🏙️ Toronto history\n🚶 Social
  walking\n📸 Exploring different neighbourhoods\n🕯️ Strange and unu
 sual stories\n😂 A good story without taking ourselves too seriously\nYo
 u don't have to be a believer.\nYou don't even have to be scared.\nJust co
 me for the walk and see what you think.\n\n###\n\n**Organizer:** Mathew\n
 📧 **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandouting
 s@hotmail.com)**\n\n### **👋 Come for the stories.**\n\n### **🚶 Stay 
 for the walk.**\n\n### **👻 And keep an eye out for who might be walking
  with us.**
