SUMMARY:🐟Walk:  Salmon Run at Humber River & James Gardens 🍂
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🐟 
 Salmon Run at Humber River & James Gardens 🍂\n\n### An Easy Fall Walk 
 — With a Pretty Amazing Natural Show Along the Way\n\nEvery fall\, somet
 hing incredible happens right here in Toronto.\nSalmon make their way upst
 ream through the **Humber River**\, battling rapids and leaping through th
 e water as they return to freshwater to spawn.\nAnd yes — you can actual
 ly see them doing it.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed\, social walk along the Hum
 ber River during salmon run season. We'll spend about 30 minutes by the ri
 ver watching for salmon before continuing along the trail toward **James G
 ardens**.\nThis isn't a difficult hike. It's a chance to get outside\, enj
 oy the fall scenery\, see something you might not normally experience in t
 he city\, and spend some time with other people along the way.\n\n✨ **Fu
 n Fact:** Some salmon travel more than 3\,000 km from the Atlantic Ocean t
 o reach freshwater rivers like the Humber. After all that distance\, they 
 still have to battle rapids and leap over obstacles to reach their spawnin
 g grounds.\nNature really doesn't mess around.\n\n📱 Don't forget to joi
 n our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbs
 Ai018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll begin 
 outside the station and make our way toward the Humber River.\nAlong the w
 ay we'll:\n\n* Walk along the Humber River\n* Stop for approximately 30 mi
 nutes to look for salmon\n* Watch the salmon making their way upstream\n* 
 Continue along the river toward James Gardens\n* Take a break at **James G
 ardens**\n* Enjoy the fall scenery and take some photos\n* Make our way ba
 ck toward the station\n\nThe walk is approximately **90 minutes**\, depend
 ing on the pace of the group and how long we spend watching the salmon.\nA
 nd remember — **the salmon are wild animals.** We can't guarantee exactl
 y how many we'll see\, or how long they'll put on a show. That's part of t
 he fun!\n\n***\n\n## 🍂 Why Come?\n\nThe salmon run is one of those stra
 nge little Toronto experiences that you can easily miss if you don't know 
 when and where to look.\nOne minute you're walking through the city. The n
 ext\, you're standing beside a river watching salmon fight their way upstr
 eam.\nWe'll also visit **James Gardens**\, one of those beautiful green sp
 aces that can make you forget you're still in Toronto.\nBring your camera\
 , bring your curiosity\, and come see what the Humber has to offer in the 
 fall.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk takes place 
 outdoors in typical Toronto fall weather.\nPlease dress appropriately for 
 the conditions and wear comfortable walking shoes. The trail may be damp o
 r muddy depending on recent weather.\nBring water and a snack\, and dress 
 in layers — fall weather can change quickly.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup De
 tails\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Right outside the station\n🫎 **Look 
 for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM**\nI will only wait
  **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:
 ** Back at the station\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in per
 son or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps su
 pport the group and allows us to continue organizing events throughout Tor
 onto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walk
 ing shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧴 Sunscreen if it's sunny\n📷 A camera or ph
 one for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great fo
 r:\n\n* Anyone who wants an easy fall outing\n* People who enjoy nature an
 d wildlife\n* Anyone curious about Toronto's rivers and green spaces\n* Pe
 ople looking for a relaxed social walk\n* Anyone who wants to meet new peo
 ple while exploring the city\n* Salmon enthusiasts — obviously. 🐟\n\n
 The activity is the container. **The people you meet along the way are the
  real experience.**\n\n***\n\n📲 **REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ah
 ead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedul
 e.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed
 \, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organize
 r: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomo
 viesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the salmon.**\n**Stay for the w
 alk.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂
 💛
